  "description": "CR 603.7, 603.12, 722.2b: whenever a land enters under alice's control, U.S.S. Farragut lets her put a creature card from her hand onto the battlefield with haste, puts it on the bottom of her library at the next end step and, when it does, draws a card; at seven charge counters, not six, it is a flying 4/4",
  "note": "Stationing from six counters with a 1-power Dwarven Trader (a 0-power Ornithopter keeps the choice a real one) makes it a creature. On turn 1 the hasty Grizzly Bears go to the library's bottom at the end step and alice draws Plains, not the Bears. On turn 3 Lightning Bolt kills the Hill Giant first, so nothing is put on the bottom and the reflexive draw never comes: after her draw step's Swamp, Island stays in the library.",
